:: R5-PostStream [release5]
<<scene "img/scenes/alone-post-stream.png" "The quiet is so loud it hums">>

The adrenaline crashes like a wave pulling back from a beach. One second I'm riding it, the next I'm sitting at my desk in the sudden silence of an offline stream, and the quiet is so loud it hums.

The ring light is still on. The webcam is off. The LED strips paint the room purple. Energy drink cans along the windowsill catch the light like a tiny city skyline.

I'm still in the outfit.

I didn't take it off. The stream ended eleven minutes ago and I'm still sitting here in the pink wig, the plaid skirt, the thigh high socks, the pastel hoodie. Jess's lip tint is slightly smeared from where I kept touching my mouth without thinking. The mascara is holding up. The concealer has faded into my actual skin tone and somehow that looks better, more natural, like the makeup is melting into me rather than sitting on top.

My phone is going nuclear. Mentions I can't scroll through fast enough. Discord notifications stacked so deep the app is lagging. DMs from accounts I've never seen. A text from LunaFrag, "Bro. BROOO. Your numbers. I can't. 😭" A DM from DuskBlade, "You might have just made the Invicta Open famous. Well played."

I catch my reflection in the dark secondary monitor. The one that's powered off. The black screen holds my image like a dark mirror. The wig. The skirt. The thigh highs. The face that isn't mine and is mine and I don't know how both of those things can be true at the same time.

I'm half hard. Have been for the last hour. I didn't notice during the stream. The adrenaline and the chat and the gameplay and the donations kept me in a state of heightened everything, and apparently everything includes arousal. Five thousand people looking at me and wanting something. The wanting was the thing. Not sexual, not all of it, but a wanting that vibrated at a frequency I've been starving for. Attention, desire, the feeling of being seen by people who liked what they saw.

I notice it now. In the silence. In the after.

My hand moves to my thigh. Slides up under the hem of the skirt. The fabric whispers against my knuckles. I stop. Fingers hovering over the shape pressing against the cotton underneath.

I pull my hand away. Stare at the donation total glowing on the primary monitor. Eight forty seven.

I stare at my reflection. The dark monitor. The wig. The lips.

My hand goes back.

