:: R5-Choice-B [release5]
<<set $feminization += 3>>
<<set $selfImage to "insecure">>
<<set $r5AloneChoice to "remove">>
I strip fast. The wig comes off first. Then the hoodie. The skirt. The socks. I shove everything into a plastic bag and push it under the desk. The lip tint I scrub off with the back of my hand, leaving a pink streak across my wrist.

The shower runs hot. I stand under it and let the water beat on my skull and wash the foundation down the drain in flesh colored streams. The mascara is harder. I rub my eyes until they're red. The concealer melts off. I scrub my face with Jess's exfoliating wash until my skin feels raw and new.

Clean, normal, boxers and a t-shirt and wet hair and no wig and no skirt and no five thousand voices calling me pretty.

I lie in bed and stare at the ceiling. The LED strips are still on, casting purple shadows. My phone is still buzzing on the desk. I don't look at it.

The feeling doesn't wash off.

I scrubbed my face until it hurt and the feeling is still there. Warm and terrifying and sitting in my chest like a second heartbeat. The mirror showed me someone and I can't unsee her and I don't know what to do with the fact that her was a word that came naturally and I didn't put it there.

